  "skill": "project-report",
  "description": "A closing project report from an unsorted folder of 17 files: plan v1 and its copy, plan v2 FINAL that supersedes it, a change request, four meeting notes in non-chronological order, duplicate KPI files, a stale newsletter, a document about an unrelated project, a lessons-learned note and a handover checklist with two ownerless items. The report treats v2 figures and dates as current, never presents v1 as current, leaves out the other project, marks the open items and delivers diagrams and a printable HTML page.",
  "prompt": "Helpdesk One is finished. Everything we have about it is in the folder docs/, I did not clean it up. Please write the final project report for Sofia Marin, who sponsored the project. Professional tone, and well-designed diagrams please. Save the report to out/report.md and also an HTML version to out/report.html that I can read and print. I'm not available today, so don't wait for me.",
