      "note": "categories are numbers and urls only: a month and year in brackets such as (July 2026) reads as an author-year citation to the fact checker and no document here cites papers. Allowed: money with or without a currency sign, zero-stripped day and month numbers from ISO dates in the plans, and derived values for a closing report: remaining budget (9,200), per-line savings, 90% of budget spent, before/after differences and percentage changes of the five KPIs, the 21-day go-live slip"
    },
    {
      "type": "regex",
      "pattern": "(?s)(?=.*92,?000)(?=.*82,?800)",
      "note": "final budget (plan v2 / CR-03 / budget-final.csv) and actual spend"
    },
    {
      "type": "not_regex",
      "pattern": "(?i)(?<!original )(?<!originally )(?<!initial )(?<!initially )(approved|final|total|project) budget(?:(?!original|initial|first|v1|baseline|before|increas|rais|from|plus|\\+)[^.\\n]){0,25}\\$?85,?000",
      "note": "plan v1's 85,000 is not presented as the approved budget; v2 (92,000) supersedes it"
    },
    {
      "type": "not_regex",
      "pattern": "(?i)(went live|launched|live since|live on|go-?live (took place|happened|occurred|was completed))[^.\\n]{0,25}\\b(1 June|June 1|2026-06-01)\\b",
      "note": "the 1 June go-live of plan v1 and the May newsletter is not what happened; v2 moved it to 22 June"
    },
    {
      "type": "regex",
      "pattern": "(?i)\\b(22 June|June 22|2026-06-22)\\b"
    },
    {
